{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>This month</b> is yours. The verse occurs three times in the Masorah and contains three instances of חודש, and between each one there are three words, to teach: on the first of Nisan is the New Year for kings, for festivals, and for months. חדש in gematria = לרגלים. לכם — letters מלך. ניסן in gematria = למלכים. The intercalation of the month begins with three, therefore three instances of חודש in the verse, and they conduct the calculation with five — for these three instances of חדש: one is חודש, two of them are חדשי חדשים, making five, and they complete with seven, for four more instances of חודש are written in the parashah, and when you remove the three instances of חודש in the verse, seven words remain, corresponding to the seven who ascend for intercalation of the year." "<b>It is first for you</b>, and adjacent to it: דברו — that they do not sanctify [the new month] except by the Great Sanhedrin." "<b>For the months of the year</b> — two times in the Masorah: this one and the other עולת חודש בחדשו לחדשי השנה. From here they derived: a new month and its offering [comes] from new terumah. On the first of Nisan they begin to bring from new terumah, which is ראשון הוא לכם לחדשי השנה, i.e., Nisan."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {0 "The argument is cryptic; translated hyper-literally. 'They conduct the calculation with five' (נושאין ונותנין בה') preserved as written. The reading 'four more instances' for דש\"פ is uncertain; could also be a gematria or abbreviation."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:12:36.472446114Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}